Date: Mon, 09 May 2016 23:54:50 +0000
Subject: calculating CI or significance at a level of a continuous variable without removing linearity assumption
Message-ID: <CAG2Vd7ib8ux+CXGsOQa3W2JurfX2S42uv0bP6UygPWe=XejKWw@mail.gmail.com>

Hi ling-R-lang-lers

I'm looking for ideas to deal with the following situation. I have an
analysis in which there's an interaction of a categorical variable,
treatment, and a continuous variable, trial.

I'd like to estimate the effect of treatment at trial = x. Specifically,
I'd lke to also calculate the CI or significance of treatment at trial = x
(so I can't just calculate the predicted effect). I'd like to do so without
giving up the linearity assumption for trial (i.e., I can't just record the
model to a simple effects specification).

I guess I could just sample from the model and calculate significance over
the samples (e.g., with the sim function from the arms package), but I feel
there should be a more straightforward way to do this, based on the
variance covariance matrices. Any ideas?

Thank you,

Florian

