Dear Florian,

My suggestion may be too simple, but couldn't you achieve this by first centering the trial number to x ?
Effects of one predictor, i.e. treatment, are estimated at the point where all other predictors are zero (hence the centering of predictors in multiple regression, and hence contrasts for categorical predictors), so this means that the effect of treatment will be estimated when I(trial-x)==0, and trial==x. This will also give you the s.e. for the treatment effect at trial==x.

m1 <- lmer( response ~ I(trial-x)*treatment ... )

(I apologise if I've misunderstood your question and if this idea is useless.)
With kind regards, Hugo Quené


